{"strongs": "H2543", "word": "חֲמוֺר", "translit": "cha.mor", "root": "חמור", "morph": "H:N", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "(he)-ass", "definition": "II. חֲמוֺר noun masculine Gen 45:23 (he)-ass (Late Hebrew id. (sometimes female, but this regularly חֲמוֺרָה ); Aramaic הֲמָרָא Arabic , Palmyrene חמרא Reckend ZMG 1888, 404 ; as imêru , Schr Cot Gloss ; — name from reddish colour) — absolute חֲמוֺר Gen 22:5 + 43 t.; חֲמֹר Exod 13:13 ; Deut 22:10 construct חֲמוֺר Exod 23:5 + 4 t.; הֲמֹר Gen 49:14 suffix חֲמֹרְךָ Deut 5:14 ; Deut 28:31 חֲמֹרֶ֑ךָ Exod 23:12 חֲמֹרוֺ Gen 22:3 + 8 t.; plural חֲמוֺרִים Judg 19:10 + 9 t.; חֲמֹרִים Gen 12:16 + 16 t.; suffix חֲמוֺרֵינוּ Judg 19:19 חֲמֹרֵינוּ Gen 43:18 חֲמוֺרֵיכֶם 1Sam 8:16 חֲמֹרֵיהֶם Gen 34:28 + 4 t.; חֲמוֺרֵיהֶם Josh 9:4 — ass (he-ass ; אתון = she-ass ) found in all periods (collective only Gen 32:6 ; Isa 21:7 ); — 1. as (valuable) property, with oxen, sheep, camels, slaves, etc. Gen 12:16 ; Gen 24:35 ; Gen 30:48 ; Gen 47:17 ; Exod 9:3 (all J ) Exod 20:17 ( E ), Exod 21:33 ; Exod 22:8 (twice in verse); Exod 22:9 ; Exod 23:4 ; Exod 23:5 ; Exod 23:12 ; Num 16:15 ; Josh 6:21 ; Josh 7:24 (all J E ); note also Exod 13:13 = Exod 34:20 ( J E ; firstlings belong to ׳ י ); Gen 36:24 ; Num 31:28 ; Num 31:30 ; Num 31:34 ; Num 31:39 ; Num 31:45 (all P ); Deut 5:14 ; Deut 5:18 ; Deut 22:3 ; Deut 22:4 ; Judg 6:4 ; 1Sam 8:16 ; 1Sam 12:3 ; 1Sam 15:3 ; 1Sam 22:19 ; 1Sam 27:9 ; 1Chr 5:21 ; Ezra 2:67 = Neh 7:68 ( Baer ), Zech 14:15 collective Gen 32:5 ( J ; || שׁוֺר ), צאֹן , עֶבֶד , שִׁפְחָה , but plural (similar ||) Gen 34:28 ( P ), Gen 47:17 ( J ); compare also יְתוֺמִים ׳ ח Job 24:3 the orphans' ass (|| שׁוֺר אַלְמָנָה ); as knowing its master's crib Isa 1:3 (|| שׁוֺר ); found in camp 2Kgs 7:7 ; 2Kgs 7:10 (both || סוּסִים ); as harnessed ׳ מֶתֶג לַה Prov 26:3 (|| סוּס ). 2. used for riding : \\ \\ a. by women Exod 4:20 ( J ), Josh 15:18 ( J E ) = Judg 1:14 ; 1Sam 25:20 ; 1Sam 25:23 ; 1Sam 25:42 , compare 2Chr 28:15 . \\ \\ b. by men 2Sam 16:2 ; 2Sam 17:23 ; 2Sam 19:27 ; 1Kgs 2:40 ; 1Kgs 13:13 (twice in verse); 1Kgs 13:23 ; 1Kgs 13:24 ; 1Kgs 13:27 ; 1Kgs 13:28 (twice in verse); Isa 21:7 ; Zech 9:9 . \\ \\ c. צֶמֶד חמורים a pair of asses 2Sam 16:1 (for burdens and for riding); for man and woman Judg 19:3 ; Judg 19:10 ; Judg 19:19 ; Judg 19:21 carrying dead body v Judg 19:28 , compare ׳ ח 1Kgs 13:29 . 3. beast of burden Gen 22:3 ; Gen 22:5 (compare v Gen 22:6 ), Gen 42:26 ; Gen 42:27 ; Gen 45:23 (all E ) Gen 43:18 ; Gen 43:24 ; Gen 44:3 ; Gen 44:13 (all J ), Josh 9:4 ( J E ), 1Sam 25:18 ; 1Chr 12:41 ; Neh 13:15 (compare also ׳ צֶמֶד ח 2Sam 16:1 above); metaphor of Issachar נָּ֑רֶם ׳ ח Gen 49:14 (poem), an ass of (strong) bones. — לֶחֶם ׳ ח 1Sam 16:20 read probably חֲמִשָּׁה five , or better עֲשָׂרָה ten , see We Dr . 4. used in tillage Isa 32:20 not to be used in ploughing with an ox ( שׁוֺר ) Deut 22:10 . 5. parts of body of ass mentioned are: ׳ לְחִי ח Judg 15:15 ; Judg 15:16 jawbone, Samson's weapon; ׳ ראֹשׁ ח 2Kgs 6:25 eaten in famine; ׳ בְּשַׂר ה Ezek 23:20 genital organ of ass (contemptuous simile) 6. ׳ קְבוּרַת ה Jer 22:19 burial of an ass , in figure of ignominious treatment of a corpse.", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2895')\">BDB2895</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2543')\">H2543</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2894')\">BDB2894</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2896')\">BDB2896</entry></div><p> II. <bdbheb>חֲמוֺר</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Gen 45:23\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(1,45,23)\">Gen 45:23</ref></sup> <highlightword>(he)-ass</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight> (sometimes female, but this regularly <bdbheb>חֲמוֺרָה</bdbheb>); Aramaic <bdbarc>הֲמָרָא</bdbarc> <placeholder1822/> Arabic <placeholder1823/>, Palmyrene <bdbheb>חמרא</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Reckend')\">Reckend<sup>ZMG 1888, 404</sup></lookup>; as <highlig